# Shell scripts MUST be committed with LF endings.
#
# The repo is worked on from Windows, where git would otherwise check
# these out (and commit them) with CRLF. A .sh file carrying CRLF runs
# fine locally and then dies on a Linux runner with the famously
# unhelpful ": command not found" -- which reads like a broken script
# rather than a line-ending problem. Vercel's ignoreCommand runs one of
# these on every push, so a CRLF slip there would fail the check and,
# because the check fails toward BUILDING, quietly restore the very
# build storm this repo added it to stop.
*.sh text eol=lf
